Gregory,

Confirming the clarification for the team and QA:

Harborline's internal target is to decide and post provisional credit by the =
7th business day after the notice of error.

This is the timing we will use in DOP-210 and DOP-211 for debit, ACH debit, Q=
uickSend, and FlexCard cases that qualify for provisional credit. The 7th bus=
iness day is an internal target only; it does not change any legal deadline o=
r the customer notice requirements in DOP-212 and DOP-230.

Operationally, analysts should continue to:
1. log the notice in ClaimTrack the same day received;
2. determine provisional credit eligibility as soon as the claim is classifie=
d;
3. post the credit in HLX Core or via Corvane workflow, as applicable; and
4. document the posting date in the case notes and correspondence queue.

QA will measure timeliness against the day the notice of error is received, u=
sing the business-day calculation in DOP-231. If the case is pending document=
ation or routing to another queue, the clock does not stop unless the procedu=
re specifically allows it.

Please use this wording in the update to the procedures set and the manager h=
uddle notes.

Luis

